   "source": {
    "label": "thm:simple",
    "number": "Theorem 1",
    "quote": "Suppose $G_t=G$ is fixed for all $T$ rounds. If we run ExpBan using the exponentially weighted forecaster and the EXP3 algorithm, then the expected regret is bounded as follows: \\sum_{t=1}^{T}g_j(t)-\\E[\\sum_{t=1}^{T}g_{i_t}(t)] \\leq 4b\\sqrt{c\\log(k)T}. For the optimal clique partition, we have $c=\\bar{\\chi}(G)$, the clique-partition number of $G$."
   },
   "confidence": "high",
   "notes": "With optimal partition c = chi_bar(G), which is NP-hard to compute in general. Regret vs any fixed action j against oblivious rewards."
  },
